  "arrangerNotes": "Verse 1, verified against the LilyPond score on French Wikipedia. 6/8 time (eighth = 0.5 beat); tied notes are played as one long note. No simplification needed. Range low 5 to 6. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums). Lyrics of the added verses: Verses 2–22: the traditional song as printed with the tune in J.-B. Weckerlin, Chansons et rondes enfantines (Garnier, 1870), pp. 58–62, from French Wikisource (https://fr.wikisource.org/wiki/Chansons_et_rondes_enfantines/Malbrough), keeping its sung liaisons and elisions (reviendra-z-à, qu'ell', nouvell's…). The refrain line keeps the verse-1 wording 'mironton, mironton, mirontaine' (Weckerlin prints 'Miron ton ton ton, mirontaine'), and the second half-line is sung three times as in verse 1. Per-verse notes (verseLines): in verse 10, 'Je l'ai vu porté-z-en terre' has 8 syllables for the 7 notes of lines 1 and 3, so the quarter note on '-brough' is played as two eighths of the same pitch.",
  "verified": true
}
